One line, turning the source-scanning test into a runtime invariant:

```ts
// http.ts, top of graphRequest
if (new URL(url).origin !== 'https://graph.microsoft.com') throw new Error('off-host request blocked')
```

Both `V1` and `BETA` already share that origin, and `laneBCore`'s `fetchPage` is bound to `graphRequest` at `laneB.ts:28`, so both nextLink loops are covered by the single check. Then `src/network.test.ts` can assert the guard exists, and SECURITY.md's sentence becomes true of the running app rather than of the repository.

